# How to cite the NCDP Data Standards. GitHub shows a "Cite this repository"
# button from this file, and Zenodo reads it when a GitHub release is archived
# (title, authors, licence, description, keywords).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the NCDP Data Standards, please cite them as below."
type: dataset
title: "NCDP Data Standards: metadata schema, naming conventions and data structure for the National Coastal Drone Programme"
version: "4.0"
date-released: "2026-10-03"      # set to the date of the GitHub release
license: CC-BY-4.0
authors:
  - family-names: Nuyts
    given-names: Siegmund
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6450-7028"
    affiliation: "Deakin University, Warrnambool"
  - family-names: Allan
    given-names: Blake
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0101-3412"
    affiliation: "Deakin University, Warrnambool"
  - family-names: Ierodiaconou
    given-names: Daniel
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7832-4801"
    affiliation: "Deakin University, Warrnambool"
  - name: "National Coastal Drone Programme (NCDP)"
    website: "https://ncdp.auscope.org.au"
repository-code: "https://github.com/NCDP-Australia/ncdp-standards"
url: "https://ncdp.auscope.org.au"
abstract: >-
  The data standards of the National Coastal Drone Programme (NCDP), a
  nationally coordinated archive of UAV (drone) coastal survey data,
  coordinated by Deakin University and funded by AuScope through the National
  Collaborative Research Infrastructure Strategy (NCRIS). They define the
  archive's directory structure and processing levels (L0 to L4), the file and
  folder naming conventions, the metadata schema (version 4.0, the archive's
  302-column survey record), the quality-assurance and quality-control
  protocol, and the templates contributors use when submitting surveys through
  the NCDP intake portal or by SFTP.
keywords:
  - coastal monitoring
  - UAV
  - drone
  - photogrammetry
  - metadata schema
  - data standards
  - FAIR data
  - Australia
  - AuScope
  - NCRIS
# After the first Zenodo release, add the concept DOI (it always resolves to
# the latest version):
# identifiers:
#   - type: doi
#     value: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"
#     description: "Concept DOI: all versions"
